WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:02.349
(engine revving)

00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:03.868
- [Narrator] Little trees.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.868
They're a rear view mirror staple,

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.078
protecting noses from offensive odors

00:00:08.078 --> 00:00:09.886
all over the world.

00:00:09.886 --> 00:00:12.219
But where do they come from?

00:00:15.546 --> 00:00:17.146
Over 60 years ago, a scientist

00:00:17.146 --> 00:00:19.026
by the name of Julius Samann

00:00:19.026 --> 00:00:21.146
had a chance encounter with a milkman

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:24.778
that changed the course of the
air freshener game forever.

00:00:24.778 --> 00:00:26.797
It was in Watertown, New York.

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:28.075
A milkman was making the rounds

00:00:28.075 --> 00:00:29.637
when he stopped to speak to Julius,

00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:31.807
a German Jewish chemist who fled the Nazis

00:00:31.807 --> 00:00:35.877
and studied alpine tree aromas
in the forest of Canada.

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:37.877
Said milkman, began venting to Julius

00:00:37.877 --> 00:00:40.437
about the stench that
spoiled milk left in his car

00:00:40.437 --> 00:00:44.218
and thus the quest began
to destroy bad car odors.

00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:46.757
Julius drew inspiration from
the tree aromas he studied

00:00:46.757 --> 00:00:50.037
by infusing their oils onto paper.

00:00:50.037 --> 00:00:53.061
In 1954, he filed a patent
for tree-shaped paper

00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:56.079
infused with odor destroying air perfume.

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:58.149
Julius then started
producing the air freshers

00:00:58.149 --> 00:00:59.588
out of an empty auto shop

00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:01.869
and sending samples to local gas stations.

00:01:01.869 --> 00:01:04.026
The little trees were a big hit,

00:01:04.026 --> 00:01:06.029
and Julius successfully created the first

00:01:06.029 --> 00:01:08.079
automotive air freshener.

00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:09.341
Though the look remains the same,

00:01:09.341 --> 00:01:11.650
the scents are forever changing.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.690
Now the little tree
company has over 60 scents

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:17.808
and has sold over a billion
little trees worldwide.

00:01:17.808 --> 00:01:20.391
(upbeat music)

